WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.076 --> 00:00:10.657
Hayley rolled on her skateboard to the top of the concrete ramp, carefully shifting her weight as she came to a stop.

2
00:00:10.658 --> 00:00:18.118
"I did it!" she thought triumphantly, before losing her balance and tumbling backward.

3
00:00:18.119 --> 00:00:21.767
A group of nearby skateboarders laughed.

4
00:00:21.768 --> 00:00:28.959
"Not even close to one of Logan's tricks," one teased.

5
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:34.788
"Where is Logan?" Hayley suddenly wondered.

6
00:00:34.789 --> 00:00:42.209
The two of them met at the skate park every Saturday—and he'd promised to help her perfect this trick today.

7
00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:47.988
She checked her phone, but his last text was from three days earlier.

8
00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:53.195
They'd made plans to meet at the library, but he hadn't shown up.

9
00:00:53.196 --> 00:01:00.026
Instead a text had arrived after midnight: "Sorry. I forgot."

10
00:01:00.027 --> 00:01:11.537
"Where are you?" she typed now. "Is everything okay?"

11
00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:18.824
On Monday in Spanish class, Señora Ramos handed back the students' graded tests.

12
00:01:18.825 --> 00:01:25.589
Hayley felt relieved to see Logan in his seat since she hadn't heard a word from him over the weekend.

13
00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:36.778
But she also felt irritated that he'd been ditching her so frequently, and today he hadn't even acknowledged her by waving or anything.

14
00:01:36.779 --> 00:01:43.015
She was about to try to catch his eye when she spotted the test on his desk.

15
00:01:43.016 --> 00:01:45.983
The grade was shocking.

16
00:01:45.984 --> 00:01:50.328
"Logan got a D?" Hayley thought.

17
00:01:50.329 --> 00:01:57.128
"What in the world is going on with him lately?"

18
00:01:57.129 --> 00:02:01.632
As the days passed, Hayley rarely saw Logan.

19
00:02:01.633 --> 00:02:04.915
"Is he avoiding me?" she wondered.

20
00:02:04.916 --> 00:02:08.920
Had she done something to offend him?

21
00:02:08.921 --> 00:02:15.921
She kept checking his online profile, and everything seemed normal.

22
00:02:15.922 --> 00:02:24.303
Then one day she spotted him sitting alone outside at a table near the guidance counselors' offices.

23
00:02:24.304 --> 00:02:29.407
"Hey, Logan," she called, "are you okay? You haven't been—"

24
00:02:29.408 --> 00:02:32.134
"I'm fine," Logan snapped.

25
00:02:32.135 --> 00:02:37.250
Provoked by his tone, Hayley heard herself snapping back.

26
00:02:37.251 --> 00:02:42.225
"There's no need to be so grouchy—I was only asking how you're doing!

27
00:02:42.226 --> 00:02:47.683
I guess you don't care that you're throwing away our friendship with your constant disappearing act.

28
00:02:47.684 --> 00:02:50.025
But if that's what you want, then—"

29
00:02:50.026 --> 00:02:59.817
"Ugh!" Logan got up and stormed off in a huff, leaving Hayley confused, angry, and utterly hurt.

30
00:02:59.818 --> 00:03:02.931
"Is something wrong, Hayley?"

31
00:03:02.932 --> 00:03:06.907
She looked up to see Mr. Obi, one of the guidance counselors.

32
00:03:06.908 --> 00:03:10.130
"No, I'm fine, but thanks for asking."

33
00:03:10.131 --> 00:03:17.704
"You don't look fine. But I'm here to listen if you feel like talking," Mr. Obi said.

34
00:03:17.705 --> 00:03:27.407
As much as Hayley didn't want to talk, she suddenly found herself blurting out all her confusion and frustration with Logan.

35
00:03:27.408 --> 00:03:31.545
She was careful, though, to avoid mentioning his name.

36
00:03:31.546 --> 00:03:36.081
Mr. Obi listened quietly until she was finished.

37
00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:41.716
"From what you've told me, it sounds like your friend may be depressed."

38
00:03:41.717 --> 00:03:48.129
A wave of guilt washed over Hayley. "I didn't think of that."

39
00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:56.179
"Depression is a common condition—in fact, one in five teens experiences it," Mr. Obi explained.

40
00:03:56.180 --> 00:04:00.911
"People with depression often feel hopeless and irritable.

41
00:04:00.912 --> 00:04:04.603
Their sleep patterns and appetites can change.

42
00:04:04.604 --> 00:04:10.148
They can also have trouble concentrating and may even lose interest in favorite activities.

43
00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:14.811
Sometimes that means they isolate themselves from friends."

44
00:04:14.812 --> 00:04:23.577
"Is there anything I can do for Lo—I mean my friend . . . if he's depressed?" Hayley asked.

45
00:04:23.578 --> 00:04:27.897
Mr. Obi nodded with a sympathetic smile.

46
00:04:27.898 --> 00:04:32.866
"You can let him know that you care, and you're available to listen.

47
00:04:32.867 --> 00:04:37.490
Try to stay in touch so your friend doesn't feel alone.

48
00:04:37.491 --> 00:04:42.218
If he won't talk to you, encourage him to talk to someone else.

49
00:04:42.219 --> 00:04:48.638
And if you ever think he's in serious trouble, you should let an adult know immediately."

50
00:04:48.639 --> 00:04:53.130
"Thanks, Mr. Obi—that information is helpful."

51
00:04:53.131 --> 00:04:58.849
Wondering how much time was left before her next class, Hayley checked her phone.

52
00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:06.302
On the screen was a new notification: Logan had posted something on his online profile.

53
00:05:06.303 --> 00:05:12.813
Hayley's hands began to tremble as she showed the counselor her phone.

54
00:05:12.814 --> 00:05:20.902
"Mr. Obi, I think Logan needs help."

55
00:05:20.903 --> 00:05:27.882
"Yes!" Hayley cheered. She had just executed the new trick perfectly.

56
00:05:27.883 --> 00:05:33.718
Even the skateboarders who usually teased her were impressed, giving her a round of applause.

57
00:05:33.719 --> 00:05:36.898
"Great job!" someone said.

58
00:05:36.899 --> 00:05:43.270
"You're here!" Hayley rolled down the ramp to greet Logan.

59
00:05:43.271 --> 00:05:47.519
"I wasn't sure if you saw my text."

60
00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:54.201
Logan nodded. "Thanks for staying in touch with me over the last few months.

61
00:05:54.202 --> 00:06:00.579
Mr. Obi reached out too—and recommended that I see a therapist.

62
00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:04.186
I'm feeling better now, except . . . "

63
00:06:04.187 --> 00:06:06.869
He looked away for a second.

64
00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:10.138
"Sorry I was a jerk to you."

65
00:06:10.139 --> 00:06:14.431
"No need to apologize!" Hayley said quickly.

66
00:06:14.432 --> 00:06:18.649
"Do you want to talk about anything?"

67
00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:25.993
Logan shook his head. "Not really—some stuff just happened at home with my parents."

68
00:06:25.994 --> 00:06:30.858
"Understood. I'm here to listen if you need it."

69
00:06:30.859 --> 00:06:38.674
"Thanks. But for now, how about we just skate?" he said before hopping on his board to perform a kick flip.

70
00:06:38.675 --> 00:06:51.838
For the first time in weeks, Hayley saw her friend smile.

